layout: layouts/base.njk
lang: en
esUrl: /politica-privacidad/
enUrl: /en/privacy-policy/
pageTitle: "Privacy policy — FerrerVersion"
pageDescription: "Privacy policy for Jorge Ferrer Gil's website (FerrerVersion): what data is collected, why, and how to exercise your rights."
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}
{% set homePath = "/en/" | url %}
<article class="legal-hero container">
  <a class="case-hero__back link-underline" href="{{ homePath }}">
    {{ icon("arrow-right") }} {{ t.nav.inicio }}
  </a>
  <h1 class="legal-hero__title">{{ t.legal.privacidad }}</h1>
  <p class="legal-hero__updated">{{ t.legal.actualizado }}</p>
</article>

<section class="container legal">
  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <p>Jorge Ferrer Gil, based in Buñol, Valencia (Spain). Contact: <a href="mailto:{{ site.contact.email }}">{{ site.contact.email }}</a>.</p>

  <h2>2. What data is collected</h2>
  <p>This site has no forms and does not collect personal data on its own. The only data processed is what you choose to send when you write through the contact channels listed on it (email, phone or WhatsApp, LinkedIn): usually your name, your contact address and the content of your message.</p>
  <p>The contact links open your own email client or app, so this data <strong>does not pass through any server belonging to this site</strong>.</p>

  <h2>3. Purpose</h2>
  <p>To reply to messages you send through the site's contact channels, for example about a job opening or one of the projects.</p>

  <h2>4. Legal basis</h2>
  <p>The data subject's consent, given by voluntarily writing through one of the contact channels (Art. 6.1.a of the General Data Protection Regulation, GDPR).</p>

  <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
  <p>Data will be kept for as long as necessary to handle your inquiry, and will not be used for a different purpose without your additional consent.</p>

  <h2>6. Recipients and data processors</h2>
  <p>Data is not shared with third parties, except where legally required. This site does not use any external service to collect contact data.</p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can exercise your rights of access, rectification, erasure, objection, restriction of processing and data portability by writing to <a href="mailto:{{ site.contact.email }}">{{ site.contact.email }}</a>, stating which right you'd like to exercise.</p>

</section>
